ize":21000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63171/S65-63171~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":21000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63171/S65-63171~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":162000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63171/S65-63171~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63198/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-12-15T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-63198 (15 Dec. 1965) --- The Gemini-7 spacecraft as seen from the Gemini-6 spacecraft during their rendezvous mission in space. They are approximately 39 feet apart. Photo credit: NASA or National Aeronautics and Space Administration","keywords":["EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)","GEMINI 6 FLIGHT","GEMINI 7 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","GEMINI SPACECRAFT","ONBOARD ACTIVITIES","PHOTOGRAPHY RENDEZVOUS"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-63198","title":"View of the Gemini 6 and Gemini 7 rendezvous"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63198/s65-63198~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1226,"size":57000,"height":1279},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63198/s65-63198~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":613,"size":11000,"height":639},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63198/s65-63198~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":613,"size":11000,"height":639},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63198/s65-63198~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1839,"size":197000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-63198/s65-63198~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61806/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-12-15T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-61806 (15 Dec. 1965) --- Astronaut Thomas P. Stafford, Gemini-6 prime crew pilot, is seen through spacecraft window as he awaits the remaining minutes of the Gemini-6 prelaunch countdown. A two-day mission in space was scheduled for astronauts Stafford and Walter M. Schirra Jr. (out of frame), command pilot. NASA successfully launched Gemini-6 from Pad 19 at 8:37 a.m. (EST) on Dec. 15, 1965. An attempt will be made to rendezvous Gemini-6 with Gemini-7. Photo credit: NASA or National Aeronautics and Space Administration","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-61806","title":"PRELAUNCH ACTIVITY (GT-6) - ASTRONAUT THOMAS P. STAFFORD - MISC."}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61806/s65-61806~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":96000,"height":853},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61806/s65-61806~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":30000,"height":426},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61806/s65-61806~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":30000,"height":426},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61806/s65-61806~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":215000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61806/s65-61806~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63209/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-12-15T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-63209 (15 Dec. 1965) --- The Gemini-7 spacecraft as seen from the Gemini-6 spacecraft during their rendezvous mission in space. The two spacecrafts are approximately 122 feet apart. This photo was taken with a modified 70mm Hasselblad camera. Photo credit: NASA or National Aeronautics and Space Administration","keywords":["HATCHES","SPACE RENDEZVOUS","STATIONKEEPING"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S65-63209","title":"Gemini-Titan (GT)-6 - Gemini 6 of 7 - Space Photography - Outer Space"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63209/S65-63209~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":251000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63209/S65-63209~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":68000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63209/S65-63209~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":68000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63209/S65-63209~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":550000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63209/S65-63209~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63220/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-12-15T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-63220 (15 Dec. 1965) --- This photograph of the Gemini-Titan 7 (GT-7) spacecraft was taken from the Gemini-Titan 6 (GT-6) spacecraft during the historic rendezvous of the two spacecraft on Dec. 15, 1965. The two spacecraft are some 37 feet apart here. Earth can be seen below. Astronauts Walter M. Schirra Jr., command pilot; and Thomas P. Stafford, pilot, were inside the GT-6 spacecraft, while crewmen for the GT-7 mission were astronauts Frank Borman, command pilot, and James A. Lovell Jr., pilot. Photo credit: NASA or National Aeronautics and Space Administration","keywords":["EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)","GEMINI 6 FLIGHT","GEMINI 7 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","GEMINI SPACECRAFT","ONBOARD ACTIVITIES","PHOTOGRAPHY RENDEZVOUS"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S65-63220","title":"View of the Gemini 6 and Gemini 7 rendezvous"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63220/S65-63220~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":191000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63220/S65-63220~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":54000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63220/S65-63220~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":54000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63220/S65-63220~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":389000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63220/S65-63220~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63189/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-12-17T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-63189 (15 Dec. 1965) --- The National Aeronautics and Space Administration's (NASA) Gemini-7 spacecraft as seen from the Gemini-6 spacecraft during their rendezvous mission in space. The two spacecraft are approximately 43 feet apart. This image was taken with a modified 70mm Hasselblad camera, using Eastman Kodak, Ektachrome (S.O. 217) color film. Photo credit: NASA or National Aeronautics and Space Administration","keywords":["GEMINI 6 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","GEMINI SPACECRAFT","GEMINI 7 FLIGHT","RENDEZVOUS"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S65-63189","title":"Gemini VI Mission Image - Rendezvous with Gemini VII"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63189/S65-63189~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":69000,"height":1274},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63189/S65-63189~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":22000,"height":637},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63189/S65-63189~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":22000,"height":637},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63189/S65-63189~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":137000,"height":1911},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63189/S65-63189~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63188/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-12-15T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-63188 (15 Dec. 1965) --- The National Aeronautics and Space Administration's (NASA) Gemini-7 spacecraft as seen from the Gemini-6 spacecraft during their rendezvous mission in space. The two spacecraft are approximately 43 feet apart. The image was taken with a modified 70mm Hasselblad camera, using Eastman Kodak, Ektachrome (S.O. 217) color film. Photo credit: NASA or National Aeronautics and Space Administration","keywords":["HATCHES","SPACE RENDEZVOUS","STATIONKEEPING"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S65-63188","title":"Gemini-Titan (GT)-6 - Gemini 6 of 7 - Space Photography - Outer Space"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63188/S65-63188~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":79000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63188/S65-63188~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":24000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63188/S65-63188~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":24000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63188/S65-63188~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":169000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-63188/S65-63188~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]}],"metadata":{"total_hits":9}}}